==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From the {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|hnot|lang=non}} from {{proto|Germanic|hnutuz|lang=is}}. Cognates with the Latin {{term|nux|lang=la}}; Old English {{term|hnutu|lang=ang}} (English {{term|nut|lang=en}}); Old High German {{term|nuz|lang=goh}} (German {{term|Nuss|lang=de}}); Danish {{term|nød|lang=da}} and Swedish {{term|nöt|lagn=sv}}.

